racle cloned sdkjs-forms into `external/sdkjs-forms`. That folder isn't covered by the factory's git exclude (only `/external/sdkjs/` is). The factory's \"uncommitted changes\" commit then added the clone as a nested-repo reference, which broke rule R2.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I took `external/sdkjs-forms` out of the repository index and moved the clone to `external/sdkjs/.theseus-addons/sdkjs-forms`, inside the excluded folder.\n- The oracle now builds with `SDK_ADDONS=../.theseus-addons/sdkjs-forms`. The build accepts any folder path here, so it doesn't need upstream's `../../sdkjs-forms`.\n- I updated `environment.md` to match, and wrote the Executor log and the friction line. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors.\n- The fix is committed on `pkt/PKT-0056`, and `git status` was clean afterwards. The total change stays within `target.files` plus the packet file and `friction.jsonl`.\n\n**Still open:** the forms clone isn't pinned to a version. If it drifts away from the pinned sdkjs, the forms suite may break.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** anything an oracle downloads has to go under a path git already ignores. `.gitignore` isn't in the target, and the factory commits any untracked files it finds.","ttft_ms":2320,"type":"result","duration_ms":170583,"uuid":"0eb06731-a3b4-4fab-8835-35063b7e2552","ttft_stream_ms":940,"time_to_request_ms":377,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":182,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":3,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":67,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":11,"request_build":18},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":175,"time_to_request_major